  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under Section 1014(a), property acquired from a decedent receives a stepped-up basis equal to the fair market value at the date of death. Drake''s estate inherits the partnership interest with a $200,000 basis, eliminating $120,000 of unrealized appreciation.
Wrong (A): The original outside basis of $80,000 is replaced by the FMV step-up at death under Section 1014. Carryover basis does not apply to inherited property.
Wrong (C): Averaging basis and FMV has no support in the Code. Section 1014 uses full FMV, not a midpoint calculation.
Wrong (D): Section 1014 replaces the decedent''s basis entirely with FMV. Allocating income through the date of death is a separate calculation under Section 706(c) that does not determine the estate''s inherited basis.$EXPL$
