Wrong (A): $85,000 adds income but ignores both the distribution and the penalty reduction, overstating basis by $10,000.
Wrong (B): $79,000 omits the $4,000 penalty reduction. Nondeductible expenses reduce stock basis even though they provide no tax deduction.
