-- Q10774: S Corporations [hard/L4]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under IRC Section 1371(b)(1), C corporation attributes such as NOL carryforwards are suspended during S years and cannot offset S corporation pass-through income. The NOL is preserved and becomes available again if the corporation reverts to C status, preventing a double benefit.
Wrong (B): The C corporation NOL cannot flow through to shareholders. Section 1371(b)(1) suspends these attributes during S corporation years.
Wrong (C): The NOL is not permanently lost. It is suspended, not extinguished, and remains available upon reversion to C status.
Wrong (D): While the BIG tax under Section 1374 may apply to built-in gains, the C corporation NOL carryforward cannot offset the BIG tax. The NOL is simply suspended.$EXPL$
