  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Section 1366, the Section 179 deduction is a separately stated item on Schedule K-1 because each shareholder must apply individual Section 179 limitations. Walsh receives 40% x $150,000 = $60,000 reported separately on her K-1.
Wrong (A): Separately stated items are not netted into ordinary business income. They pass through individually so shareholders can apply personal limitations under Section 179(b).
Wrong (C): The Section 179 deduction does appear on the K-1 as a separately stated item. While it does reduce AAA, it must be reported to each shareholder for individual-level limitation.
