  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Section 1368, distributions from an S corporation reduce stock basis but cannot reduce debt basis. Palmer''s $30,000 stock basis absorbs $30,000 tax-free, reducing stock basis to zero. The excess $15,000 is treated as capital gain from the deemed sale of stock.
Wrong (A): Distributions never reduce debt basis. Only pass-through losses may be deducted against debt basis under Section 1367(b)(2).
Wrong (C): Stock and debt basis cannot be combined to absorb distributions. Section 1368 limits tax-free treatment to stock basis only.
Wrong (D): The excess is capital gain, not a taxable dividend. Dividend treatment under Section 1368(c) applies only when the S corporation has accumulated C corporation E&P.$EXPL$
