-- Q10779: S Corporations [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under the S corporation loss limitation tiers, losses must not exceed stock and debt basis (Section 1366(d)), then must not exceed the at-risk amount (Section 465). Dixon''s $100,000 stock basis passes the first test, but the at-risk amount is only $70,000 because the $30,000 nonrecourse related-party loan is excluded. The $20,000 excess is suspended.
Wrong (A): $90,000 ignores the at-risk limitation under Section 465, which caps the deduction below the stock basis amount.
Wrong (C): $100,000 is the stock basis, not the deductible amount. The at-risk rules impose a tighter limit than the basis test.
Wrong (D): $60,000 understates the at-risk amount. Dixon is at-risk for $70,000, not $60,000.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 10779;

-- Q10782: S Corporations [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under IRC Section 469, S corporation losses from activities in which the shareholder does not materially participate are passive losses, deductible only against passive income. Preston''s $60,000 basis exceeds the $50,000 loss, but the passive activity rules limit the current deduction to $10,000 of available passive income. The remaining $40,000 is suspended.
Wrong (A): $50,000 ignores the passive activity limitation. Although basis is sufficient, Section 469 restricts the deduction to passive income.
Wrong (B): $0 incorrectly assumes no deduction is available. Preston has $10,000 of passive income from another source to offset.
Wrong (D): $60,000 is Preston''s stock basis, not the deductible loss amount. The loss is $50,000, further limited to $10,000 by the passive rules.$EXPL$
