Wrong (A): Only $10,000 of basis was restored, so only $10,000 of the $15,000 suspended loss becomes deductible. The full amount requires sufficient basis.
Wrong (C): There is no expiration period for basis-limited suspended losses. They carry forward indefinitely until basis is restored or stock is disposed of.
