  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under IRC Section 1374(c)(2), the net recognized built-in gain for any year cannot exceed the NUBIG reduced by gains recognized in prior years. Atlas had $300,000 NUBIG and recognized $200,000 in Year 2, leaving $100,000. In Year 3, only $100,000 of the $180,000 gain is subject to the 21% BIG tax.
Wrong (B): Each year''s gain is not independently assessed. The cumulative NUBIG cap limits total BIG tax exposure across all recognition period years.
Wrong (C): There is no two-year lookback exception to the five-year recognition period. The BIG tax applies throughout the statutory period.
Wrong (D): Pro-rata annual allocation has no basis in the Code. The cap is computed cumulatively, not ratably over the recognition period.$EXPL$
