  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under IRC Section 1361(c)(4), differences in voting rights among shares of common stock do not create a second class of stock. An S corporation may have voting and nonvoting shares as long as all shares confer identical economic rights.
Wrong (A): Differences in distribution rights would create a prohibited second class of stock because they affect the economic rights that the single-class rule protects.
