-- Q10801: C Corporations [hard/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under IRC Section 304(a)(1), when a person controlling two corporations sells stock of one to the other, the transaction is recharacterized as a distribution under Section 301. The $200,000 from Alpha is taxable as a dividend to the extent of both corporations'' combined E&P.
Wrong (B): Section 304 specifically overrides sale treatment. Capital gain recognition is unavailable because the transaction is recharacterized as a distribution.
Wrong (C): The $200,000 is not a tax-free return of capital. Section 304 treats it as a dividend to the extent of E&P, preventing extraction of earnings at preferential rates.
Wrong (D): Section 351 nonrecognition does not apply here. Section 304 governs related-corporation stock transfers and takes priority.$EXPL$
